{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/tally.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T14:03:53.085751Z","id":"cdf205d42d48fc39bbcec3c20a61c161c8417f2d056048a2e9bba1381e66f5e5","body":{"detail":"`clax_bot::clax::Tally` is exported because `ClaxProvider::begin` in crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs (157-159) calls `Tally::of(cx.history)`. Inside the crate its readers are the tick (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs 1052) and crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs 217 and 554. It is the crate's own integration test reading the crate's own type, so no crate turns on another's features and the layering is as it was; but it makes the provider's private fold part of what clax-server and clax-worker can name. When the `clax` provider lives in `crates/clax-bot/src/clax/` and the proof drives it instead of its own adapter, make `Tally`, its fields and `Tally::of` `pub(crate)`. The adapter's old fold and this one agree on every history the proof builds: asserted equal in `begin` with a temporary assertion (base and `created` from every step with a payload, against `Tally::of`), all of `//crates/clax-bot:all` passed. They differ only where a step that is not a script carries `created: true`, which no tick writes. The proof still fails without `created` (`seam::a_script_after_one_that_created_an_artifact_may_not_create_another`).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":37},"content_hash":"4b5d1115070aa2816829bdff9d21e8efb761960aedc557d8f3856e6f3f0662b1"},"summary":"`Tally` and its six fields are `pub` for one reader outside the crate, the proof's adapter in tests/seam.rs","tags":["t3","for-t5","review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/tally.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T16:22:01.584199Z","id":"be4a1e68494cbb3bf7aa07a8255211109e1e22fc75ebad670d922df8ccf095d4","body":{"detail":"The fold's readers are the tick (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs, `Tick::clax`) and `ClaxProvider::begin` (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs), which takes `base` and `created` from `Tally::of(cx.history)`. crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs has no adapter and names no `Tally`; `clax::tally` is a private module and `clax` exports `ClaxProvider` alone. `bazelisk build --config=clippy --output_groups=clippy_checks //crates/clax-bot/...` passes. Proposed close: fixed.","kind":"comment","references":"cdf205d42d48fc39bbcec3c20a61c161c8417f2d056048a2e9bba1381e66f5e5","summary":"`Tally` and `Tally::of` are `pub(crate)`: the provider that reads them is in this crate","tags":["t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T16:22:01.596247Z","id":"6f5a08aa3fc639961950f83934a437773526798f0288aa3a5b180a1d946e2a73","body":{"detail":"Recorded again where the code now is (it was record b7a2cda0c5f3fc510f0905fd7e9e21c0d97a64ef6bc36c1f1a8d743d0316f004 on crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs, a file that moved). A fetch of a URL the run's page store keeps answers from the store even when the fetch cap is reached, because spec 2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools §6.2 says such a fetch does not count against the fetch cap. Checking the cap first would refuse later windows of a page the run already paid for with web_cap. Tests: crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs the_second_window_comes_from_the_store, a_stored_page_is_served_at_the_fetch_cap.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":675},"end":{"line":700},"content_hash":"edb9dabc23726a743971332f3760e638b8beabcea31ae864c26caf366bbfc067"},"summary":"The page store is checked before the run's cap, not after it","tags":["t5","revisit:the cap is meant to bound reads of stored pages too","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T16:22:01.596293Z","id":"c70dda80ac5e8d1e4a9ca1261383538ebf22eba7f6ff0b5b33018ecfe83f6887","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs still calls `BotHost::working` (before a turn or a script, and after each terminal commit) and posts every notice itself (`notify_at`). crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs calls no provider's `working`: row 1 of the step table in surface.rs says so. For the change that moves the endings: the run loop calls `working`, `ending` and `ended` for every binding; the conformance fixture of this provider (crates/clax-bot/tests/providers.rs) then has an `ending` that can fail and notices to read, and the two cases it names as not applicable are played; and a run whose scripts reach another surface (crates/clax-bot/tests/generic.rs) still ends with Clax's notices on Clax's threads, because only its script step is generic.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":165},"end":{"line":171},"content_hash":"4bbea682b0fceba2dff6b9e5f9883525e18cb40bc5eff616f5d905b19fce3974"},"summary":"Clax's provider does nothing in `working`, `ending` and `ended`: the roster and the notices are still the run loop's","tags":["t5","for-t7","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T16:22:01.596550Z","id":"f568a9a7148f4402ac45b96d2f7033d2b3ad22553343217c47d6f92290a3ca47","body":{"detail":"`api::Performer`: this match, by which a session finds the part that performs an operation; `host::check_op` (crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs), for a `BotHost`'s own check; the table and its tests in api.rs; and the reference. `Deps::host`: run.rs (the roster's `working`, the notices' `plan_reply`, the request's `context`), driver.rs (`start_waiting`) and `ClaxProvider::of`. `Deps::web`: `ClaxProvider::of` alone. A provider that names its own operations (a match on the operation's name here) frees `Performer`; `Deps::host` and `Deps::web` go when the tick is given its providers and the roster and notices are theirs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":85},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"3112b5ac304ee179058eedc91c555550952cae4eb53b7282672bc3915157f265"},"summary":"What still reads `api::Performer`, `Deps::host` and `Deps::web`","tags":["t5","for-t10","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T16:22:01.596594Z","id":"785c9e30c896757cdde2a5925e67644cf602e520e4b17c7ebbbb7c8fdd4a85e8","body":{"detail":"Before, the web performer made the journal entry itself and, when it could not (`run_not_claimed`), answered with no `cost_milli`. Now the refusal is the run loop's to journal (`Answer::refused(…).uncharged()`), made before any entry is, so its `call` event carries `cost_milli: 0` whether or not the row could be written. The attempt is abandoned either way (the claim is lost), no step commits it, and no test reaches it: crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs loses no claim. Keeping the old event would cost a read of the run for each such refusal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":143},"end":{"line":149},"content_hash":"b0e0986ed9da8efb6925a4a43cef570716545935c360f3fc0ea3327ac9a4e9ae"},"summary":"A refusal of check 2 made while the driver no longer holds the run shows a cost of 0 in its event, where the code before the seam showed none","tags":["t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T16:52:12.563931Z","id":"7b719df59cc1d709cda14e1c9433fd90f7a39dfa7e68140fa4d3dda0fc7766d0","body":{"detail":"A sandbox that lets another driver take the run before the script's first call, with a script that calls `clax.web.fetch` in a run that did not declare `fetch`, and in one that declared it on a host with no source (a test added to a scratch copy of crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs). The reference's `call` event: `{\"code\":\"run_not_claimed\",\"ok\":false,\"op\":\"web.fetch\",\"ms\":0,\"web\":{\"url\":…}}`, no `cost_milli`. The seam's: `{\"code\":\"web_disabled\",\"cost_milli\":0,…}`. Both for both halves of check 2; no journal row either way; both ticks end `Waiting(NotOurs)`. The reason is in crates/clax-bot/src/script_reference/web.rs 464-472: the reference made the journal entry before it looked at whether the refusal was check 2's, and answered the entry's failure. So the script's own `catch` sees another code too, and the sentence in crates/clax-bot/src/surface.rs 163-166 (\"shows `cost_milli: 0` … where the code before the seam … showed no cost\") and \"What the script is thrown … did not change\" (159-161) hold only while the driver has the run. Who can see it: someone with the run's panel open on the live stream (`EventHub::emit` broadcasts an attempt's events as they are made, crates/clax-bot/src/events.rs 272-310) sees that call until the next attempt's `step_started` replaces the step; nothing stores it, no step commits it, and the model is never told. The entry also fails when the read of the run's row fails (`Store::call_entry`, crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs 1498) with the claim held: then the step does commit, with `web_disabled` in its `calls` and in what the model is told where it had the store's error. To make it identical: `ClaxSession::web` makes the entry before check 2 and answers `unwritten` when it cannot (the read the reference made too), which covers the declared half; the undeclared half is answered by `SurfaceProvider::undeclared`, which is given no claim, so the core would have to make an entry before it asks the hook. The other refusals of the core (arguments that do not hold) were always answered as themselves whatever the entry did (crates/clax-bot/src/script_reference.rs 365-374), so the seam's answer is the consistent one.","kind":"comment","references":"785c9e30c896757cdde2a5925e67644cf602e520e4b17c7ebbbb7c8fdd4a85e8","span":{"start":{"line":143},"end":{"line":149},"content_hash":"b0e0986ed9da8efb6925a4a43cef570716545935c360f3fc0ea3327ac9a4e9ae"},"summary":"Reproduced, and it is more than the cost: the script is answered `web_disabled` where the code before the seam answered `run_not_claimed`","tags":["verify-t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/tally.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:14:15.997719Z","id":"669d3cf55974a761a785f19f29e64ee3127e1ba68eeecbd8e2b3ec953591d899","body":{"detail":"`clax_bot::clax::Tally` is exported because `ClaxProvider::begin` in crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs (157-159) calls `Tally::of(cx.history)`. Inside the crate its readers are the tick (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs 1052) and crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs 217 and 554. It is the crate's own integration test reading the crate's own type, so no crate turns on another's features and the layering is as it was; but it makes the provider's private fold part of what clax-server and clax-worker can name. When the `clax` provider lives in `crates/clax-bot/src/clax/` and the proof drives it instead of its own adapter, make `Tally`, its fields and `Tally::of` `pub(crate)`. The adapter's old fold and this one agree on every history the proof builds: asserted equal in `begin` with a temporary assertion (base and `created` from every step with a payload, against `Tally::of`), all of `//crates/clax-bot:all` passed. They differ only where a step that is not a script carries `created: true`, which no tick writes. The proof still fails without `created` (`seam::a_script_after_one_that_created_an_artifact_may_not_create_another`).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":37},"content_hash":"1521962e2743a77a0bace237b50a13bcf0bb67403f6f9430723d168fa81330cb"},"summary":"`Tally` and its six fields are `pub` for one reader outside the crate, the proof's adapter in tests/seam.rs","supersedes":"cdf205d42d48fc39bbcec3c20a61c161c8417f2d056048a2e9bba1381e66f5e5","tags":["t3","for-t5","review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:14:16.225004Z","id":"a602eba5b172fa2513aa86530003ce76602286f14868fa91cef18c03ea45a198","body":{"detail":"Before, the web performer made the journal entry itself and, when it could not (`run_not_claimed`), answered with no `cost_milli`. Now the refusal is the run loop's to journal (`Answer::refused(…).uncharged()`), made before any entry is, so its `call` event carries `cost_milli: 0` whether or not the row could be written. The attempt is abandoned either way (the claim is lost), no step commits it, and no test reaches it: crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs loses no claim. Keeping the old event would cost a read of the run for each such refusal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"b0e0986ed9da8efb6925a4a43cef570716545935c360f3fc0ea3327ac9a4e9ae"},"summary":"A refusal of check 2 made while the driver no longer holds the run shows a cost of 0 in its event, where the code before the seam showed none","supersedes":"785c9e30c896757cdde2a5925e67644cf602e520e4b17c7ebbbb7c8fdd4a85e8","tags":["t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:14:16.456886Z","id":"285218bc68466d1025cdd5d54e4571cd8f62d9458686a10d0f42b5f2e46ef010","body":{"detail":"Recorded again where the code now is (it was record b7a2cda0c5f3fc510f0905fd7e9e21c0d97a64ef6bc36c1f1a8d743d0316f004 on crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs, a file that moved). A fetch of a URL the run's page store keeps answers from the store even when the fetch cap is reached, because spec 2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools §6.2 says such a fetch does not count against the fetch cap. Checking the cap first would refuse later windows of a page the run already paid for with web_cap. Tests: crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs the_second_window_comes_from_the_store, a_stored_page_is_served_at_the_fetch_cap.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":678},"end":{"line":703},"content_hash":"edb9dabc23726a743971332f3760e638b8beabcea31ae864c26caf366bbfc067"},"summary":"The page store is checked before the run's cap, not after it","supersedes":"6f5a08aa3fc639961950f83934a437773526798f0288aa3a5b180a1d946e2a73","tags":["t5","revisit:the cap is meant to bound reads of stored pages too","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:14:22.680124Z","id":"454b9a36fdb17df4f5061f4bb91bdfe8dc701aee7df51a9cf58fb614bd2981c4","body":{"detail":"`policy` reads `self.tick.clax.created` (217) and `Tick::script` reads `self.clax.base` (554). Both are `clax::Tally` fields (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/tally.rs 21-37), folded by the tick (run.rs 1052). A `clax` session opened by `SurfaceProvider::begin` should fold them itself from `StepCx::history`, as the proof's adapter now does with the same function (crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs 159), and the tick's copy then has no reader in this file. `Tally::of` reads only steps whose `committed_at` is set; `StepCx::history` is documented as the committed steps (surface.rs 606-610), and the tick's `steps` may hold a second uncommitted step if a run ever had two (only the first is taken out as `open`, run.rs 1041-1044), so pass the slice as it is and let the fold filter. Mutations that show both reads are held: 554 as `self.run.base_version` fails `golden::resumed::a_script_after_a_publish_is_resumed_from_the_published_version` and `seam::a_script_after_a_rebase_starts_from_the_version_rebased_onto`; 217 without the tally's `created` fails `rules::a_brief_run_creates_one_artifact` and `golden::scripts::a_second_artifact_is_refused`.\n\nRecorded again where the code now is: it was record 7564590a4493710cb151474667f770e3c09df7943ba45796371ac003bf16eaed on crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs, whose lines moved to this file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":147},"end":{"line":148},"content_hash":"6d8ae587df767f4b4d0cb20618cf56c2ea4b0ef14a847a74dc2598a4cbb0cef3"},"summary":"For the change that moves script.rs behind the seam: the two reads of `Tick::clax` here (217, 554) become the clax session's own `Tally::of(cx.history)`","tags":["t3","for-t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:14:24.083263Z","id":"70a0f3e01dc4e6ae5a75116d137c99e1f6dc440621ac28e2f465d3c652966eb8","body":{"detail":"It decides whether a web call's audit record keeps the provider's response whole or by hash. It bounds no run and the model reads none of it, so it is not among `RunLimits` (crates/clax-bot/src/policy.rs:91); it is a limit of the web surface's own, and moves with the web performer.\n\nRecorded again where the code now is: it was record f7cbc515f60afe885145fd0d4c2ef407c88e89a5dbb4403361691a3f20514979 on crates/clax-bot/src/script/web.rs, whose lines moved to this file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":234},"end":{"line":234},"content_hash":"d92a55cc832e824030ea87b64f387e29c4f8a17a1dcc1e218747e9551542fc47"},"summary":"`AUDIT_RESPONSE_BYTES` (64 KiB) is a size compiled into the web performer","tags":["for-t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:14:56.201507Z","id":"9d48f43bcaa15c28c3a7528ee441c79a4058e07ce5aca0e2e177adbbe95ce65c","body":{"detail":"A sandbox that lets another driver take the run before the script's first call, with a script that calls `clax.web.fetch` in a run that did not declare `fetch`, and in one that declared it on a host with no source (a test added to a scratch copy of crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs). The reference's `call` event: `{\"code\":\"run_not_claimed\",\"ok\":false,\"op\":\"web.fetch\",\"ms\":0,\"web\":{\"url\":…}}`, no `cost_milli`. The seam's: `{\"code\":\"web_disabled\",\"cost_milli\":0,…}`. Both for both halves of check 2; no journal row either way; both ticks end `Waiting(NotOurs)`. The reason is in crates/clax-bot/src/script_reference/web.rs 464-472: the reference made the journal entry before it looked at whether the refusal was check 2's, and answered the entry's failure. So the script's own `catch` sees another code too, and the sentence in crates/clax-bot/src/surface.rs 163-166 (\"shows `cost_milli: 0` … where the code before the seam … showed no cost\") and \"What the script is thrown … did not change\" (159-161) hold only while the driver has the run. Who can see it: someone with the run's panel open on the live stream (`EventHub::emit` broadcasts an attempt's events as they are made, crates/clax-bot/src/events.rs 272-310) sees that call until the next attempt's `step_started` replaces the step; nothing stores it, no step commits it, and the model is never told. The entry also fails when the read of the run's row fails (`Store::call_entry`, crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs 1498) with the claim held: then the step does commit, with `web_disabled` in its `calls` and in what the model is told where it had the store's error. To make it identical: `ClaxSession::web` makes the entry before check 2 and answers `unwritten` when it cannot (the read the reference made too), which covers the declared half; the undeclared half is answered by `SurfaceProvider::undeclared`, which is given no claim, so the core would have to make an entry before it asks the hook. The other refusals of the core (arguments that do not hold) were always answered as themselves whatever the entry did (crates/clax-bot/src/script_reference.rs 365-374), so the seam's answer is the consistent one.","kind":"comment","references":"a602eba5b172fa2513aa86530003ce76602286f14868fa91cef18c03ea45a198","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"b0e0986ed9da8efb6925a4a43cef570716545935c360f3fc0ea3327ac9a4e9ae"},"summary":"Reproduced, and it is more than the cost: the script is answered `web_disabled` where the code before the seam answered `run_not_claimed`","supersedes":"7b719df59cc1d709cda14e1c9433fd90f7a39dfa7e68140fa4d3dda0fc7766d0","tags":["verify-t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:16:38.552330Z","id":"764a6add48725e68941adf2f99fd3f5b0282a054b4dc99e72792b67542ad154d","body":{"detail":"Kept: a refusal the run loop can make without the store is made without it. crates/clax-bot/src/surface.rs (\"When the entry cannot be made, the answer itself differs\") states both cases. (1) Another driver holds the run: the script is thrown `web_disabled` and the live `call` event shows that code and `cost_milli: 0`, where the code before the seam threw and showed `run_not_claimed` with no cost; nothing is journaled or committed and the tick waits `NotOurs`. Pinned by `web::a_web_operation_a_run_lacks_is_refused_as_itself_when_the_claim_is_lost` (crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs, both halves of check 2) and, as the second named exception in the header of crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs, by `a_refusal_at_check_2_is_made_without_the_store`, which holds the reference to its event and the seam to its own. Changed one at a time: the refusal with no cost shown fails `golden::web::the_journal_rows_of_web_operations_a_run_lacks_are_pinned`, `script_differential::a_refusal_at_check_2_is_made_without_the_store` and 5 more; the session making the entry before check 2 and answering its failure fails `script_differential::a_refusal_at_check_2_is_made_without_the_store`, `web::a_web_operation_a_run_lacks_is_refused_as_itself_when_the_claim_is_lost`. (2) The store fails to read the run's row while the driver holds the run (`Store::call_entry`): the step commits with `web_disabled` and `cost_milli: 0` in its `calls` and in what the model is told, where it committed the store's error, and the refusal has no row. Not pinned: `clax_store::Store` has no way for a test to make one read fail (no fault hook; removing the run's row fails the commit too). Pinning it takes a store that a test can make fail one read, which belongs with the change that gives the tick its providers. The owner's to confirm: this is the second place this step changes something a person can observe, beside the journal row of record 964e0fd9.","kind":"comment","references":"a602eba5b172fa2513aa86530003ce76602286f14868fa91cef18c03ea45a198","summary":"Both cases are stated, the lost claim is pinned on the product path and as a named exception of the comparison, and the committed case cannot be driven: for the owner, the second observable change of this step","tags":["t5","fix-round","status:needs-decision","for-t8","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:45:38.105865Z","id":"e9eaa9fb6021e03f93353642746adfee58b30c62c74466e44a3120f9630b74f8","body":{"detail":"A sandbox whose host, around the script's first call, lets another driver take the run (clock forward 61 seconds, `Store::claim_run` by a new driver) and after the call takes it back for the tick's own driver (61 seconds more, `claim_run` again). The journal entry of that call cannot be made (`run_not_claimed`), and the step then commits, since the driver holds the run again and no one began the step meanwhile. Run in a scratch copy of crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs at 65a77a602, with a script that calls `clax.web.fetch` and returns what it caught, for a run that did not declare `fetch` and for one that declared it on a host with no source. The reference's committed step: `calls: [{\"code\":\"run_not_claimed\",\"ok\":false,\"op\":\"web.fetch\",…}]` with no `cost_milli`, and the model is told `[\"run_not_claimed\",\"driver drv_… does not hold run …; claim it again\"]`. The seam's: `code: web_disabled`, `cost_milli: 0`, and the model is told `[\"web_disabled\",\"clax.web.fetch is not available to this run\"]`. No journal row either way. So the decided answer is what a model is told in the one case where a step commits it, and it is the better one: the reference told the model a driver's ID. crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs `a_web_operation_a_run_lacks_is_refused_as_itself_when_the_claim_is_lost` (1612) pins the attempt that is abandoned; the committed one is unpinned.","kind":"comment","references":"a602eba5b172fa2513aa86530003ce76602286f14868fa91cef18c03ea45a198","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"b0e0986ed9da8efb6925a4a43cef570716545935c360f3fc0ea3327ac9a4e9ae"},"suggested_fix":"Add the committed case beside that test with the sandbox above, asserting the step's `calls` entry and what the model is told.","summary":"The case that commits can be driven with the test store, with no fault hook: the claim taken and taken back within the one call","tags":["verify-t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T17:52:39.873904Z","id":"34796d01db522ed3533bf1486c1b504ff22153f1b80a444f73b1c14b5c1a8203","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs, `a_web_operation_a_run_lacks_is_refused_as_itself_in_a_step_that_commits`: a sandbox whose host lets another driver take the run around the script's first call and takes it back for the tick's driver after (`LosesTheRunForACall`), for a fetch the run did not declare and for one it declared on a host with no source. The step commits with `calls: [{op: web.fetch, ok: false, code: web_disabled, cost_milli: 0, web: {url}}]`, the script's value is `[\"web_disabled\", \"clax.web.fetch is not available to this run\"]`, and the step has no journal row. crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs, `a_refusal_at_check_2_is_committed_as_itself`, holds the reference to what it committed in the same run (`run_not_claimed`, no cost, a message that begins `driver drv_`) and the seam to its own. crates/clax-bot/src/surface.rs (\"When the entry cannot be made\") and the comparison's header say so. `bazelisk test //crates/clax-bot:all --runs_per_test=3` passes. Still for the owner: whether this answer, the second thing this step changes that a person or a model can observe, stands.","kind":"comment","references":"a602eba5b172fa2513aa86530003ce76602286f14868fa91cef18c03ea45a198","summary":"The step that commits the refusal is pinned, on the product path and in the comparison, by the method of reply e9eaa9fb; what is left undriven is a read of the run's row failing with the claim never lost","tags":["t5","fix-round","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T18:44:21.881501Z","id":"12824206ce6bdc39405aef25f774c3ce53beb68db6964ad921545921f642e73f","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/ending.rs: `show_working` and `run_ended` call `BotHost::working`, `run_ending` posts the notices (`post`, at `StepCx::notice` places, each a `plan_reply` run with `Claim::entry`), applies the finish rule over `Tally::of(cx.history)` and reads the sources. The run loop calls the three hooks for every binding (crates/clax-bot/src/ending.rs, `Tick::working`, `Tick::end`). The conformance fixture of this provider (crates/clax-bot/tests/providers.rs, `claxs_own_provider_passes_the_provider_conformance_suite`) now plays the terminal cases: its `noticed` probe reads the journal rows at the terminal step's notice places and the replies in the store, an `ending` armed to fail after it posted is made again, and a fake beside the provider records the hooks for `lifecycle`; one case is left as not applicable (the unwritten failure). The notice is on the thread once after `ending` was called for four attempts, and `ended` told twice turns the roster off twice and changes no reply. A run whose one surface is the fake's (crates/clax-bot/tests/generic.rs) ends with no reply on a thread and no call to the host: `a_run_of_the_fake_alone_finishes`, `_gives_up`, `_is_cancelled`, `_is_stopped_by_a_cap`, `_fails`.","kind":"comment","references":"c70dda80ac5e8d1e4a9ca1261383538ebf22eba7f6ff0b5b33018ecfe83f6887","summary":"Clax's provider now does the roster, the notices, the finish rule, the sources and the follow-ups in `working`, `ending` and `ended`","tags":["t7","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/ending.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T18:44:21.885295Z","id":"02eec7eb4f4d4800d66e49fddbf35c2e0e7549d020237d52ed80306adb7fd225","body":{"detail":"The notice of thread `i` is journaled at the same place whatever the end (`StepCx::notice(i)`), and a step begun again keeps its number. A `stopped` or `give_up` step that posted its notice and then could not be committed `max_commit_failures` times becomes the `failed` step under the same number: the `failed` notice is another call at a place the journal holds, and is refused there. Seen with the fake, whose `ending` answers `key_reused` (`generic::an_ending_that_fails_is_counted_and_bounded_and_the_other_binding_is_still_asked`); for `clax` the entry is made by `Claim::entry` over `Store::call_entry` and was not driven here, and it was the same before the endings moved (the run loop posted both at `NOTICE_SEQ + i`). The thread then holds the first notice and the run ends `failed` with the failure's words in its payload only. No golden covers a terminal step whose commit fails after its notice was posted (the `failed` goldens fail a script step, which posts none).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":167},"content_hash":"6637c0fcf6ea434dde7cce6a059ab9d29965d82f8d6efcd79d6c414f6f3bd0e1"},"summary":"A terminal step that ends as another kind than its earlier attempts keeps their notice places, so its notice may be refused the key and not posted","tags":["t7","for-t8","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/ending.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:38:58.352682Z","id":"dbd92c1402d4bf20dcf666adbf9a28305bf5e3c738bed97eb977176d3c94a636","body":{"detail":"`posted` is set from the rule alone (line 202), as the run loop did before the move (crates/clax-bot/src/ending_reference.rs 223, 241) and as crates/clax-bot/src/surface.rs's table says (`posted` is true whenever the rule held, whether or not a post succeeded). Changing line 202 to `json!(post && every post succeeded)` (each `self.post` returning whether all its replies were made) passes `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:all`: no golden or comparison run has a finish whose summary post fails. The field is stored in the step's payload and nothing in the product reads it today, so a change there would be silent.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":191},"end":{"line":202},"content_hash":"74a1d3a54c0ee1603e7f71b65cde3f599028c63d0cd36f92bca1d08d1439e2f7"},"suggested_fix":"A `finish` on two threads whose second reply cannot be planned (move the thread off the run's artifact, as the review probe did with `UPDATE threads SET artifact_id` under `PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF`), pinning `posted: true` and one reply.","summary":"No test holds that a finished step's `posted` is the finish rule whatever came of the posts","tags":["review","test-gap","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/ending.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:38:58.353476Z","id":"1296adde916cffa2ab552e5fbd8c0769c6847a9afca1d9410f0e2512f5a2d5c0","body":{"detail":"A probe test added to crates/clax-bot/src/ending_differential.rs and removed after: a run on one thread with ClaxBot turned off, a SQLite trigger refusing the commit of any `stopped` step (`BEFORE UPDATE OF committed_at ON bot_steps WHEN OLD.kind = 'stopped'`), driven to its end both ways. Both end `failed`, the thread holds one reply (the stop's notice), and what the two leave (`Left`: run, steps, journal, events, audit, usage, writes, calls, replies, roster) is equal. `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:clax_bot_lib_test --test_arg=probe_` passed. The journal keys a reply by run, step and place, not attempt (crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs `with_bot_journal`), before the move and after it.","kind":"comment","references":"02eec7eb4f4d4800d66e49fddbf35c2e0e7549d020237d52ed80306adb7fd225","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":167},"content_hash":"6637c0fcf6ea434dde7cce6a059ab9d29965d82f8d6efcd79d6c414f6f3bd0e1"},"summary":"Driven for `clax`: a `failed` step after a posted stop notice posts nothing of its own, through the seam and through the reference alike","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/ending.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T20:07:27.532403Z","id":"7fdbd3471c874a7f9d9454da0177a221594d23166e32b9682e9275b39a0a064a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"02eec7eb4f4d4800d66e49fddbf35c2e0e7549d020237d52ed80306adb7fd225","summary":"Not changed by holding the run's `RunInfo` and providers: the notice places are the binding's and the step's number, which did not move; still open","tags":["t8","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T20:07:27.532734Z","id":"84923db596ebf1f981e94963644b0f84b220270dd85a44f7f05492c2c617f5ca","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a602eba5b172fa2513aa86530003ce76602286f14868fa91cef18c03ea45a198","summary":"Not changed: the web session and its refusals were not touched by the tick holding its providers; still for the owner","tags":["t8","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T23:59:19.585787Z","id":"5c41a158fbcbf6646a6b618b93366aacf7c753057742999ad3523fa3f9feeb23","body":{"detail":"Commits ac72d8527 and 359f0c1f4; see the reply on record d311ae86 (crates/clax-bot/src/registry.rs). `host::host_op` (crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs) checks that the operation is one of src/clax.d.ts with the access asked. Left open for the owner to close.","kind":"comment","references":"f568a9a7148f4402ac45b96d2f7033d2b3ad22553343217c47d6f92290a3ca47","span":{"start":{"line":85},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"7c64c4ec37072d9b071617065da0502686ca4854cd798312e8cffe6eb54bbaa4"},"summary":"Done: the session names its own operations (`PARTS`, `Part`), and `api::Performer`, `Deps.host` and `Deps.web` are gone","tags":["t10","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:03.325472Z","id":"f6bc4e8fec82aa61650c6347e56085d7883e14c313a264c3dbd60876e980a10c","body":{"detail":"`policy` reads `self.tick.clax.created` (217) and `Tick::script` reads `self.clax.base` (554). Both are `clax::Tally` fields (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/tally.rs 21-37), folded by the tick (run.rs 1052). A `clax` session opened by `SurfaceProvider::begin` should fold them itself from `StepCx::history`, as the proof's adapter now does with the same function (crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs 159), and the tick's copy then has no reader in this file. `Tally::of` reads only steps whose `committed_at` is set; `StepCx::history` is documented as the committed steps (surface.rs 606-610), and the tick's `steps` may hold a second uncommitted step if a run ever had two (only the first is taken out as `open`, run.rs 1041-1044), so pass the slice as it is and let the fold filter. Mutations that show both reads are held: 554 as `self.run.base_version` fails `golden::resumed::a_script_after_a_publish_is_resumed_from_the_published_version` and `seam::a_script_after_a_rebase_starts_from_the_version_rebased_onto`; 217 without the tally's `created` fails `rules::a_brief_run_creates_one_artifact` and `golden::scripts::a_second_artifact_is_refused`.\n\nRecorded again where the code now is: it was record 7564590a4493710cb151474667f770e3c09df7943ba45796371ac003bf16eaed on crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs, whose lines moved to this file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":170},"end":{"line":171},"content_hash":"6d8ae587df767f4b4d0cb20618cf56c2ea4b0ef14a847a74dc2598a4cbb0cef3"},"summary":"For the change that moves script.rs behind the seam: the two reads of `Tick::clax` here (217, 554) become the clax session's own `Tally::of(cx.history)`","supersedes":"454b9a36fdb17df4f5061f4bb91bdfe8dc701aee7df51a9cf58fb614bd2981c4","tags":["t3","for-t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:03.498738Z","id":"605dcd1c00f980ef5797e5a87538ef7afa971998e2db061f0dacd722b67c93f0","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs still calls `BotHost::working` (before a turn or a script, and after each terminal commit) and posts every notice itself (`notify_at`). crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs calls no provider's `working`: row 1 of the step table in surface.rs says so. For the change that moves the endings: the run loop calls `working`, `ending` and `ended` for every binding; the conformance fixture of this provider (crates/clax-bot/tests/providers.rs) then has an `ending` that can fail and notices to read, and the two cases it names as not applicable are played; and a run whose scripts reach another surface (crates/clax-bot/tests/generic.rs) still ends with Clax's notices on Clax's threads, because only its script step is generic.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":188},"end":{"line":208},"content_hash":"b98a54081114280cbb82dee794235753f257b363e8a6fd67bdb34ad194813be2"},"summary":"Clax's provider does nothing in `working`, `ending` and `ended`: the roster and the notices are still the run loop's","supersedes":"c70dda80ac5e8d1e4a9ca1261383538ebf22eba7f6ff0b5b33018ecfe83f6887","tags":["t5","for-t7","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:03.668669Z","id":"8320f2cf8d7130eda31cd5a453323a0ae3f6a7b060213b2cdbc71aab3002f540","body":{"detail":"`api::Performer`: this match, by which a session finds the part that performs an operation; `host::check_op` (crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs), for a `BotHost`'s own check; the table and its tests in api.rs; and the reference. `Deps::host`: run.rs (the roster's `working`, the notices' `plan_reply`, the request's `context`), driver.rs (`start_waiting`) and `ClaxProvider::of`. `Deps::web`: `ClaxProvider::of` alone. A provider that names its own operations (a match on the operation's name here) frees `Performer`; `Deps::host` and `Deps::web` go when the tick is given its providers and the roster and notices are theirs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":138},"end":{"line":142},"content_hash":"bf1684f5785655048d7101e7c4e6fa8a75f9e20c1bff1d031c3c83cd8072c39e"},"summary":"What still reads `api::Performer`, `Deps::host` and `Deps::web`","supersedes":"f568a9a7148f4402ac45b96d2f7033d2b3ad22553343217c47d6f92290a3ca47","tags":["t5","for-t10","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/ending.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:15.715113Z","id":"8d9526d05ac474387a3a423118d738f9919e267082bbf4aa2b62dec38e84431c","body":{"detail":"`stop_lead` has a notice for each: 'this Clax could not work out what this run may do', 'this Clax could not put together what to send the model', 'the model took longer to answer than this run allows'. The first two end the run `failed`, the third `stopped`. None is reachable under `DefaultPolicy` (no fixture under crates/clax-bot/tests/golden changes), and none is pinned by a fixture; the run view and the HTTP run JSON show `reason` as they show any. When the endings move behind a provider's `ending`, these reasons go with `End::Failed` and `End::Stopped` and the words become the provider's; whoever first ships such a policy pins them.\n\nRe-recorded unchanged from record 23d65d69 on crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs, whose subject moved here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":59},"end":{"line":75},"content_hash":"200a2a2652746f83ba212641529e22974fa196fc37d7e28c7544d872bee2eb6a"},"summary":"Three endings a person can see only under a policy that is not the default, with words nobody chose: `policy_error`, `policy_history_<n>` and `model_timeout`","tags":["for-t7","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/ending.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:16.727657Z","id":"cdc6baabf39228a966f9c1cd77f434e0562a00999bc0410a694188b12d3dd008","body":{"detail":"`what_i_did` (1374-1396) reads `clax.scripts`, `clax.changed` and `clax.published`; `finish` reads `clax.replied` (1574). They are the only readers of those four `clax::Tally` fields (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/tally.rs 21-37), so when the notices and the posting rule move into the provider's `ending`, it folds `Tally::of(cx.history)` there and these reads go. `scripts` is in the tally although a script step is the core's and docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-11-claxbot-surfaces-step2.md (\"Where the nouns are read\", Core) lists it with the core's fields: its one reader is the notice's wording (\"I ran 2 scripts\"), and `history::Control` (crates/clax-bot/src/history.rs 86-99) holds only what the tick decides by. A provider that is not `clax` and wants the count folds it from the steps' kinds. Held: `clax: Tally::default()` at run.rs 1052 fails 25 integration tests, `golden::endings::a_notice_counts_the_scripts_that_ran` among them; 1574 without `replied` fails `golden::endings::finish_posts_no_summary_on_any_thread_when_the_run_replied_on_one`.\n\nRe-recorded unchanged from record e90edb8f on crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs, whose subject moved here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":80},"end":{"line":101},"content_hash":"1657820bb3b6071503997d51979097102a92b417e031f6d7063baeb5d98d06c0"},"summary":"For the change that moves the endings behind `ending`: `what_i_did` and the finish rule read `Tick::clax`, and the count of scripts is in the tally, not in the core's fold","tags":["t3","for-t7","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:20.246630Z","id":"e44906117bbe90a86bb17433bc01292276a818fb96139ae002e39205a37647e2","body":{"detail":"`policy` reads `self.tick.clax.created` (217) and `Tick::script` reads `self.clax.base` (554). Both are `clax::Tally` fields (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/tally.rs 21-37), folded by the tick (run.rs 1052). A `clax` session opened by `SurfaceProvider::begin` should fold them itself from `StepCx::history`, as the proof's adapter now does with the same function (crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs 159), and the tick's copy then has no reader in this file. `Tally::of` reads only steps whose `committed_at` is set; `StepCx::history` is documented as the committed steps (surface.rs 606-610), and the tick's `steps` may hold a second uncommitted step if a run ever had two (only the first is taken out as `open`, run.rs 1041-1044), so pass the slice as it is and let the fold filter. Mutations that show both reads are held: 554 as `self.run.base_version` fails `golden::resumed::a_script_after_a_publish_is_resumed_from_the_published_version` and `seam::a_script_after_a_rebase_starts_from_the_version_rebased_onto`; 217 without the tally's `created` fails `rules::a_brief_run_creates_one_artifact` and `golden::scripts::a_second_artifact_is_refused`.\n\nRe-recorded unchanged from record 7564590a on crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs, whose subject moved here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":168},"end":{"line":171},"content_hash":"6b3ae9ea2f79eb1ad2baa17775c07b4ff2f4187e34a0a23f16d8632096698d61"},"summary":"For the change that moves script.rs behind the seam: the two reads of `Tick::clax` here (217, 554) become the clax session's own `Tally::of(cx.history)`","tags":["t3","for-t5","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:57:28.928027Z","id":"b8e71a2cec89ce672794e3030882a91f62d4301879f4eaf4b67834ba96d79318","body":{"detail":"Every script the proof runs is step 2 of its run, after one turn: `tally` (seam.rs 102-111) always answers `(None, false)` and `begin` (145-163) always loads the draft at the run's own base. Changes made one at a time and run with `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration --test_arg=seam::` (7 tests): (1) seam.rs 148 loads the draft at `run.base_version` whatever `tally` answers: all 7 pass. (2) seam.rs 238 drops `self.created_before`: all 7 pass. (3) seam.rs 320 never refuses a second publish in one script: all 7 pass. (4) seam.rs 215 hands `OpCtx::new` another attempt: all 7 pass (the fake host does not read it; crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs 633 does). The same changes made to today's code and run against the whole of `//crates/clax-bot:integration` (175 tests): script.rs 217 without `self.tick.hist.created` fails `golden::scripts::a_second_artifact_is_refused` and `rules::a_brief_run_creates_one_artifact`; script.rs 301 fails `golden::scripts::the_draft_operations_answers_are_pinned`; but script.rs 554 as `let base = self.run.base_version;` passes all 175, the seam's 7 among them, and passes `//crates/clax-bot:all`, `//crates/clax-server:all` and `//crates/clax-worker:bot_test` too. No test runs a script after a step that published or rebased: crates/clax-bot/tests/rules.rs 143-197 rebases and publishes in the run's last script. So the change that moves script.rs 554-555 into a provider's `begin` can load every later script's draft at the run's first base (a second publish then conflicts, and a script after a rebase reads the old files) and pass the proof and every fixture under crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/.\n\nRe-recorded unchanged from record 487f98c0 on crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs, whose subject moved here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":168},"end":{"line":186},"content_hash":"6e87a4939198b0a2f01dfb9625d7c55ecf0b5ef98da47adfe2e665538ec87d3d"},"suggested_fix":"A proof case, and a fixture for today's path, in which a first script publishes (and another in which it rebases) and a second script reads a file, writes and publishes: the second step's draft, its `if_version` and its `payload.base` compared on both paths. For a brief's run, a second script that calls `artifacts.create` after a first that created one.","summary":"No proof case opens a session over a history that moved the draft's base or created an artifact, so what `begin` folds from the committed steps is unproved, and for the base no other test of clax-bot holds it either","tags":["review","seam","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/ending.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-13T06:23:26.961644Z","id":"ad1c32d41976b459fa4d74f779a95fe0ff4fba5a035373bcbcdeab4e325a093e","body":{"detail":"run_ending passes `run.key_source == Instance` to notice(). The run routes also hide a stop whose error_detail.key_source is \"instance\" (crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs without_instance_failure). A person who turns use_own off mid-run, after a run recorded on their own key was made, gets a stop on the instance's key whose notice says \"I stopped: the model provider refused the key.\" (lead in crates/clax-bot/src/clax/ending.rs) instead of INSTANCE_PROVIDER_LEAD. It is Clax's wording, never the provider's, so nothing the provider said leaks. run_ending is not given the stop's core fields, which hold the call's key.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":203},"end":{"line":204},"content_hash":"08c7b8ef63a0233b8612c47672209d440c764496b9933781775be7c09128ae42"},"suggested_fix":"Pass the stop's error_detail.key_source (or the ending's core fields) to run_ending and decide by it, falling back to run.key_source.","summary":"The thread notice picks the instance key's wording from the run's stored key_source, not from the key the failing call ran on","tags":["claxbot","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/ending.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-13T06:23:26.961741Z","id":"b22bc0505f9345e05af3199b6a582c3df565250de5bda9b9fc6f05d153b87d27","body":{"detail":"On the instance's key every stop for key_rejected or model_error says INSTANCE_PROVIDER_LEAD (\"This is a problem with how this Clax is set up, not with your request\"), and the run panel says the same (web/shell/src/bot/model.ts instanceProblemWords). model_error also covers 400 invalid_request refusals such as \"prompt is too long\" that a long thread or a large attachment causes, where trying again later fails the same way. The stored error_detail.class (invalid_request vs auth vs api) would let Clax say \"ClaxBot could not finish this request; try a shorter one\" for those without quoting the provider; the server would then pass a coarse `kind` beside `busy` in instance_problem (crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs without_instance_failure).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":104},"end":{"line":110},"content_hash":"a5af607bf40c4f42e5b929b0b39f71c35a211ac14c99577607d135af96210e28"},"summary":"Should a refusal the request itself caused (a prompt too long, an image too large) still be told as a problem with how this Clax is set up?","tags":["claxbot","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:38:30.819647Z","id":"e7cdbd4272c81229985b1d2727e55ef8b0c56982d750ce0a8d1a0609da70c645","body":{"detail":"BrowserAccess::now grants browse when browser.browse.enabled is on and the person's web choice is too, and Task 14 of docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser.md writes NewRun::browser from that shape, so such a run's prompt declares browse while every call of it is refused. Task 20 (browse egress, the URL rule) replaces this refusal; the branch must not merge with browse declarable and unperformed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":342},"end":{"line":347},"content_hash":"1be3a976cf4151e9a340a60db1c4a51d90c2e2da2540a7d98dcdfe4fafdb39df"},"summary":"clax.browser.browse is refused browser_disabled after the grant check: no build performs it yet, though a run whose admin turned browsing on declares it","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:38:30.819695Z","id":"37a0dda6f5d9c326e0ee4dc089c5b14d907d6e822c12e0016f2662a2db922e92","body":{"detail":"A ClaxSession has no RunLimits and no HubLimits: the provider holds SessionLimits { image_side: policy::DEFAULT_IMAGE_SIDE } (ClaxProvider::new) and clax/browser.rs keep_screenshot passes ContentLimits::default() to put_bot_content. A RunPolicy with a smaller image_side would leave a screenshot out of what the model is shown (images::choose says why) instead of it being taken smaller, and a daemon whose [bot] content limits are lower than the defaults holds browser screenshots to the defaults.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":59},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"741576b2d8af95e6426cbf93e0f0a623dbb9d9e64c0fcff2196e21d9cecdde45"},"suggested_fix":"Give the provider the run's limits (a field set by the driver or from RunPolicy) and the hub's ContentLimits when the daemon wires it (Task 14).","summary":"A browser test's screenshots are scaled to DEFAULT_IMAGE_SIDE (8000), not to the run's RunLimits::image_side, and kept under ContentLimits::default(), not the hub's configured content limits","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:54:47.732932Z","id":"51dac953231fd803ec0bf7fbbf3d7e5f59a9129c5526e12a04652d8ad8bd5dd1","body":{"detail":"browser_ctx (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:512-513) refuses credits_exhausted unless the person can pay price(timeout_s * 1000). That pre-check rests on spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md §8.2: the time cap 'bounds what this call can cost' so 'a test cannot run a person past their week'. But tested() charges whole_seconds(closed_at - opened_at) with no upper bound. The deadline (browser.rs:406-408) fires timeout_s after the open, and run_test (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs:303-305) still sends Target.disposeBrowserContext and Browser.close and closes the socket before it reads closed_at. So every test that hits its deadline measures a little over timeout_s, and rounding up to the whole second makes the charge at least timeout_s + 1 s: 61 s for the default 60 s cap. A test that finishes its steps just under the cap can also round past it. The person can then pay more than the pre-check allowed, and the script's `cost` and `left.credits` say so. No test drives the clock past the deadline at the Spend level: crates/clax-bot/tests/browser.rs advances the ManualClock by 8.4 s at most.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":551},"end":{"line":562},"content_hash":"01869c9fc8be6d9cb93eb41c8d2936addb7d2f808f426c273f29e1c4cab40f42"},"suggested_fix":"Charge min(whole_seconds(ms), timeout_s * 1000) in tested(), or pre-check a bounded close allowance on top of the cap, and say which in the module docs. Add a run-level test whose fake advances the clock past the deadline and asserts that the usage row's qty is at most timeout_s * 1000.","summary":"A browser test can be charged more than the time cap its credits pre-check priced: the measured time is never capped at timeout_s","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:54:47.733013Z","id":"9603c59fbb5c8d4740bdf7faf8646c53df192f3e6d4c2f0c4eeaced9686d9ba4","body":{"detail":"run_test marks a screenshot step only by its value, {\"screenshot\": <index>} (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs:1097). An eval step's value is whatever the page's expression returns by value (session.rs:623, then 686-691 put it in the step's `value`), so the page controls it. tested() takes every step whose value[\"screenshot\"] is a u64 to be a screenshot step. If a page's eval answers {screenshot: 0} and the test also took a screenshot, the eval step's value becomes the first screenshot's Image handle. If that screenshot could not be kept, the eval step is rewritten to {ok: false, error} and the whole result is set passed: false. The script, the journal entry and the run panel's step counts (summarize) then all show the wrong outcome.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":579},"end":{"line":591},"content_hash":"79d509dbc61bf7cfbc7eca1e4c527a3ff568641617049fc2ae98e5123b4dc868"},"suggested_fix":"Have run_test name the screenshot steps outside the values: for example TestRun::shot_steps: Vec<(step_index, shot_index)>, filled where session.rs:1096-1097 pushes the shot. Or match each step index against opts.steps[i] being the screenshot variant. Rewrite only those steps in tested().","summary":"Screenshot steps are found by the shape of a step's value, so an eval step whose page returns {screenshot: <n>} gets a screenshot handle in place of its value, or is failed","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:02.510732Z","id":"679a27dfc717fdc0dba6b8656830ec728f157dbd8016355653c5f1676175251c","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:512-513 pre-checks price(&rate, ks, timeout_s * 1000). browser.rs:551-554 (qty at 554) charges qty = whole_seconds((closed_at - opened_at) ms), and whole_seconds (browser.rs:224-226) rounds up with no min() against the cap. crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs:303-305: run_test calls d.close() (Target.disposeBrowserContext, Browser.close, transport close; session.rs:1101-1127) and only then reads closed_at, so a test that ran to its deadline (browser.rs:406-408, timeout_s after the deadline was set) measures the close on top and rounds up to timeout_s + 1 s. Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md section 8.2 (lines 564-571) states the cap 'bounds what this call can cost'. crates/clax-bot/tests/browser.rs advances the clock 4.2 s (line 105) and 61 s only for the replay test (line 191), which opens no browser; no test charges past the cap. Concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"51dac953231fd803ec0bf7fbbf3d7e5f59a9129c5526e12a04652d8ad8bd5dd1","summary":"confirmed: the charge is whole_seconds(closed_at - opened_at) with no cap at timeout_s, while the pre-check prices timeout_s * 1000","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:02.511176Z","id":"68dd0c5f8d86603b3a3169858ba24c9d1bdc0a2bfd247e97df80071431f35ee6","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:579-591 rewrites every step with step[\"value\"][\"screenshot\"].as_u64(), replacing the value with kept[i] or the whole step with {ok: false, error} and setting passed false (592-594). crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs:993-1000: Step::Eval answers the page expression's JSON as the step value, and session.rs:686-691 stores it in r[\"value\"], so a page returning {screenshot: 0} has the same shape as a screenshot step's value (session.rs:1097). Nothing else marks screenshot steps: TestRun (session.rs:198-206) carries only shots, opened_at, closed_at and outcome. Concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"9603c59fbb5c8d4740bdf7faf8646c53df192f3e6d4c2f0c4eeaced9686d9ba4","summary":"confirmed: tested() treats any step whose value has a u64 'screenshot' as a screenshot step, and an eval step's value is page-controlled","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T08:14:25.844513Z","id":"6007e54b13851829bea9eb7c415d41288a8c73f2ac8fa3bccc189d0a7b67df5e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5add704ef","summary":"Fixed in 5add704ef: tested() charges min(whole seconds, timeout_s * 1000); the integration test browser::a_failure_after_opening_is_charged_at_most_the_time_cap_and_counts (65 s measured, 60 s cap) records 60,000 and passes. bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... //crates/clax-store/... //crates/clax-server/... //crates/clax-cli/... //bazel/wasm:check //web:unit //web:lint //web:typecheck //web:bundle_size: 33 tests pass (run at 835edf396; //crates/clax-bot/... passes again after the rustfmt commit da686e589).","supersedes":"51dac953231fd803ec0bf7fbbf3d7e5f59a9129c5526e12a04652d8ad8bd5dd1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T08:14:26.214174Z","id":"3a1011e730704f474b34c606c43166dad72629d431610a6add3313895c97c7be","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:305fb1cbd","summary":"Fixed in 305fb1cbd: tested() rewrites only steps whose options.steps entry is Step::Screenshot; browser::an_eval_value_shaped_like_a_screenshot_stays_a_value passes. bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... //crates/clax-store/... //crates/clax-server/... //crates/clax-cli/... //bazel/wasm:check //web:unit //web:lint //web:typecheck //web:bundle_size: 33 tests pass (run at 835edf396; //crates/clax-bot/... passes again after the rustfmt commit da686e589).","supersedes":"9603c59fbb5c8d4740bdf7faf8646c53df192f3e6d4c2f0c4eeaced9686d9ba4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T08:57:07.304041Z","id":"cf9378c9d9c778219fe909a0366051bb94581a6ea5a602ee4d85c31761ee4c11","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e7cdbd4272c81229985b1d2727e55ef8b0c56982d750ce0a8d1a0609da70c645","summary":"No run declares browse now: start_run writes the browser shape through run_browser_shape (crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs), which leaves browse out whatever browser.browse.enabled says; pinned by tests/api_claxbot_run.rs a_run_started_with_browser_on_declares_it. The branch may merge with this refusal in place; Task 20 lifts both together. Proposed close once Task 20 lands or is cut.","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T08:57:07.304503Z","id":"aa0d16914108d4a0540a1108286cde8eeb252deb257a5061a0a5cc241d800aaf","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"37a0dda6f5d9c326e0ee4dc089c5b14d907d6e822c12e0016f2662a2db922e92","summary":"The content half is addressed: ClaxProvider::with_content_limits and Deps::with_content_limits carry the host's limits, the daemon passes its hub's (state.bot_surfaces.limits().content_limits(), crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs driver_with_sources), and keep_screenshot puts screenshots under them; tests/browser.rs screenshots_are_kept_under_the_hosts_content_limits. The image_side half stays open: browser_limits is still DEFAULT_IMAGE_SIDE.","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T09:50:06.546261Z","id":"a4f464fdbb634fc1395387e488073cb9b5172f9ea8115f63a9fe7a8f6f92529d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3609b254a","summary":"clax.browser.browse is performed (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs browse); crates/clax-bot/tests/browser.rs a_browse_opens_its_url_and_is_charged_as_a_browse and the other browse tests pass. bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... //crates/clax-store/... //crates/clax-server/... //crates/clax-cli/... //bazel/wasm:check //web:unit //web:lint //web:typecheck //web:bundle_size //apps/clax_app:prompt_sync: 34 tests pass","supersedes":"e7cdbd4272c81229985b1d2727e55ef8b0c56982d750ce0a8d1a0609da70c645","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T09:59:47.666514Z","id":"bfe72f994c57e037933cc07e55d39fdd3703da8cd853637d739fef62f4328b91","body":{"detail":"clax_bot_js::QuickJs::run (crates/clax-bot-js/src/lib.rs, the `tokio::select! { biased; () = cancel.cancelled() => None, r = host.ask(&op, args) => Some(r) }` around each host call) drops host.ask's future as soon as the run's CancelToken fires; run.rs `watched` fires the same token on a Stopping run and on a lost claim. ClaxSession::browser -> open_and_run -> run_test is that future, so its own cancellation handling (Cdp sees the token, Driver::end cuts \"time\", Driver::close sends Target.disposeBrowserContext and Browser.close) never runs: the transport is dropped mid-await, then `tested` and `write_browser` never run. Result: no bot_calls row, no browser.time usage, no bot.browser audit record, nothing in the run panel, and Browser Run keeps the browser until its keep_alive (10 s, crates/clax-server/src/browser_source.rs KEEP_ALIVE_MS) lapses. This contradicts the module docs of this file (lines 56-59: charged 'whatever it answered: a result, a timeout, a cancellation') and spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md §5.4 (a cancellation after the page loaded answers partial and is charged) and §8.2. After a lost claim the next driver runs the step again with no entry and opens a second browser. browser::session's cancellation tests drive run_test directly with a token, never through the sandbox, and crates/clax-bot/tests/browser.rs has no cancel case, so nothing catches it. StepSession::call's contract (crates/clax-bot/src/surface.rs, 'The call's future may be dropped at any await') allows the drop, so the provider must survive it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":531},"end":{"line":572},"content_hash":"9a14412faf484b549b43e422d6842d89f62902e769c9a79d02fdb4e94d01ae8c"},"suggested_fix":"Make the browser call survive its future being dropped: run open_and_run + tested + write_browser in a task the session spawns (clax_rt spawn, or a guard whose Drop sends Browser.close on the transport and journals a charged `cancelled` entry with the time measured so far), and let the session future await that task. Add a tests/browser.rs case that cancels the run while clax.browser.test is past the load (the FakeChrome holds a step) and asserts one charged, counted row and Browser.close sent.","summary":"On the QuickJS sandbox a cancelled run (or a lost claim) drops a browser call's future: Browser.close is never sent, and an opened browser is never charged, journaled, audited or shown","tags":["review","review:browser-final","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:04:00.502286Z","id":"eb77aaab34baa8b3929c86de56a63730ad1a6bbded971c43afd5cddf1e9be090","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot-js/src/lib.rs:513-516 is `tokio::select! { biased; () = cancel.cancelled() => None, r = host.ask(&op, args) => Some(r) }`, then returns Cancelled (:541-554). crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs:1095-1118 (watched) cancels the same token on Stopping and on a lost lease. The chain host.ask -> StepHost::ask (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs:214-254) -> surface::dispatch -> perform -> session.call(call).await (crates/clax-bot/src/surface.rs:1694) -> ClaxSession::browser (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:270-293) has no spawn: `grep -rn 'spawn(' crates/clax-bot/src` finds only driver.rs:617 (the driver loop). write_browser runs only after browser_fresh returns (:291-292). The only Drop on the transport is Slot's (crates/clax-server/src/browser_source.rs:301-306), which frees the count and sends nothing; ClaxSession::finish (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/session.rs:160-183) does nothing about browsers. crates/clax-bot/src/surface.rs:2144 allows the drop. `grep -n cancel crates/clax-bot/tests/browser.rs` finds nothing.","kind":"comment","references":"bfe72f994c57e037933cc07e55d39fdd3703da8cd853637d739fef62f4328b91","span":{"start":{"line":531},"end":{"line":572},"content_hash":"9a14412faf484b549b43e422d6842d89f62902e769c9a79d02fdb4e94d01ae8c"},"summary":"confirmed: a cancel drops the browser call's future, and nothing closes, journals or charges it","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:23:25.260136Z","id":"fb2ec7d0a2e96a3aa91377622ceeaa05c6f47e7696aeda34256db2e1a7a4581e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:39989daef","summary":"A guard (Opened) armed once the browser opens journals, charges, counts and audits the time so far, answered cancelled, when the call's future is dropped; the socket's drop ends the session (Browser.close cannot be sent from a drop, so Browser Run ends the browser after its 10 s keep-alive). crates/clax-bot/tests/browser.rs a_run_cancelled_while_the_browser_is_open_is_charged_its_time cancels the run through the QuickJS sandbox while the page's load is held: it failed before (no browser.time row) and passes after, with one 3,000 ms row, one counted test and one bot.browser record (ok false, code cancelled).","supersedes":"bfe72f994c57e037933cc07e55d39fdd3703da8cd853637d739fef62f4328b91","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:25:15.839451Z","id":"a395ac41f19b8452ef897ca131981f4f5ed3f97a07e950984faf7bb22be4ed50","body":{"detail":"A ClaxSession has no RunLimits and no HubLimits: the provider holds SessionLimits { image_side: policy::DEFAULT_IMAGE_SIDE } (ClaxProvider::new) and clax/browser.rs keep_screenshot passes ContentLimits::default() to put_bot_content. A RunPolicy with a smaller image_side would leave a screenshot out of what the model is shown (images::choose says why) instead of it being taken smaller, and a daemon whose [bot] content limits are lower than the defaults holds browser screenshots to the defaults.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":60},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"741576b2d8af95e6426cbf93e0f0a623dbb9d9e64c0fcff2196e21d9cecdde45"},"suggested_fix":"Give the provider the run's limits (a field set by the driver or from RunPolicy) and the hub's ContentLimits when the daemon wires it (Task 14).","summary":"A browser test's screenshots are scaled to DEFAULT_IMAGE_SIDE (8000), not to the run's RunLimits::image_side, and kept under ContentLimits::default(), not the hub's configured content limits","supersedes":"37a0dda6f5d9c326e0ee4dc089c5b14d907d6e822c12e0016f2662a2db922e92","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/spend.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T19:06:55.648245Z","id":"360169087ad793b4a344bec8644d63b6891959c7a7fd85f9ce5a9c9b280e990e","body":{"detail":"Recorded again where the code now is: it was record a602eba5 on crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs (check 2's refusal), which moved here as spend::disabled for every charged call, web and browser alike. The refusal is the run loop's to journal (Answer::refused(...).uncharged()), made before any entry is, so its call event carries cost_milli: 0 whether or not the row could be written. The attempt is abandoned either way (the claim is lost), no step commits it, and no test reaches it. Keeping the old event would cost a read of the run for each such refusal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":313},"end":{"line":326},"content_hash":"ea3fcc1476218ca1affc0c20fa1d6f1dde7d114d07cdb59516945777a0097a7f"},"summary":"A refusal of step 2 made while the driver no longer holds the run shows a cost of 0 in its event, where the code before the seam showed none","tags":["t5","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T19:06:55.649450Z","id":"32589555b90c3cd1c487fdf894186ba4dbb25d9673fb7159633336ed8c0c9cff","body":{"detail":"It decides whether a search's bot.spend record keeps the provider's response whole or trimmed. It bounds no run and the model reads none of it, so it is not among RunLimits (crates/clax-bot/src/policy.rs); it is a limit of the web surface's own, and moves with the web performer. Re-anchored after the Spend path moved the performer's code (commit 91de6f4a7).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":114},"end":{"line":116},"content_hash":"2bd3a7fd210c42b9e598a581c9f44b2cc45735e7da2b18c33c6e93b9ae941d8f"},"summary":"`AUDIT_RESPONSE_BYTES` (64 KiB) is a size compiled into the web performer","supersedes":"70a0f3e01dc4e6ae5a75116d137c99e1f6dc440621ac28e2f465d3c652966eb8","tags":["for-t5","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/spend.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T19:06:56.239494Z","id":"d4af66f34654b30290184b7ccc1991c404c295916a3bf1227ab20f4e69cfea1b","body":{"detail":"Recorded again where the code now is: it was record 285218bc on crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs; the order is now the Spend sequence's, step 6 (free answers) before step 7 (cap), spec 2026-11-19-claxbot-browser §4.6. A fetch of a URL the run's page store keeps answers from the store even when the fetch cap is reached, because spec 2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools §6.2 says such a fetch does not count against the fetch cap. Checking the cap first would refuse later windows of a page the run already paid for with web_cap. Tests: crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs the_second_window_comes_from_the_store, a_stored_page_is_served_at_the_fetch_cap.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":427},"end":{"line":439},"content_hash":"001d239baca282e2d9741a9a070102b9aa9a9a54922ed0ac028e57cf59a65ba0"},"summary":"The page store is checked before the run's cap, not after it","tags":["t5","revisit:the cap is meant to bound reads of stored pages too","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T19:06:56.240719Z","id":"e5849e8e050962ac7b0b97c666db2a22301be70bfec3d1b9ac12b57870933986","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:91de6f4a7","summary":"Moved: check 2's refusal is now spend::disabled (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/spend.rs), where the same concern is recorded again with its detail.","supersedes":"a602eba5b172fa2513aa86530003ce76602286f14868fa91cef18c03ea45a198","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T19:06:56.849972Z","id":"57b868b1ba62efb7705debec748c38bcaed8931d7a9a090a6e068f27e5f46fc5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:91de6f4a7","summary":"Moved: the order of the page store and the cap is now the Spend sequence's (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/spend.rs, steps 6 and 7), where the same alternative is recorded again.","supersedes":"285218bc68466d1025cdd5d54e4571cd8f62d9458686a10d0f42b5f2e46ef010","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T22:57:05.850443Z","id":"76b42ae82a56e5ce2e1bae4cdb6ba0d113b913e263414b6b09cea4b99615da2d","body":{"detail":"Doing it needs the run's limits on the step (StepCx) and a per-call image side in CallCtx, since one registry serves every run of the host.","kind":"comment","references":"a395ac41f19b8452ef897ca131981f4f5ed3f97a07e950984faf7bb22be4ed50","summary":"Still open after 167dfeeef: live sessions take their SessionLimits from the provider's registry (ClaxProvider::with_browser builds BrowserSessions with browser_limits, DEFAULT_IMAGE_SIDE), and neither StepCx nor ClaxSession carries the run's RunLimits, so a session's screenshots are not scaled to RunLimits::image_side","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T00:29:52.986615Z","id":"da9517e9d3683835eb523f8e3b4d0f90112fcb84b97161c8da3ef9f43015438f","body":{"detail":"Not cheap: the image side would have to travel per call (a field of browser::live::CallCtx) from the run's limits, which StepCx does not carry (crates/clax-bot/src/surface.rs StepCx::new has no limits; the run loop's RunLimits stay in run.rs). Under DefaultPolicy RunLimits::image_side is DEFAULT_IMAGE_SIDE anyway, so only a policy that lowers it is affected.","kind":"comment","references":"a395ac41f19b8452ef897ca131981f4f5ed3f97a07e950984faf7bb22be4ed50","summary":"Still open after 98d0d0400: the daemon's one registry (crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs browser_sessions, 1282-1301) is built with SessionLimits { image_side: DEFAULT_IMAGE_SIDE } and serves every run, so a run's own RunLimits::image_side cannot reach it there either","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T02:55:31.443054Z","id":"edb71d2035255c73906261f4a948629ff06f9492a2d52ec500db0b2b2b27faf0","body":{"detail":"A ClaxSession has no RunLimits and no HubLimits: the provider holds SessionLimits { image_side: policy::DEFAULT_IMAGE_SIDE } (ClaxProvider::new) and clax/browser.rs keep_screenshot passes ContentLimits::default() to put_bot_content. A RunPolicy with a smaller image_side would leave a screenshot out of what the model is shown (images::choose says why) instead of it being taken smaller, and a daemon whose [bot] content limits are lower than the defaults holds browser screenshots to the defaults.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":60},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"bc56c5a666492218b59bc0827d3316d166be87fe5ac66ccfc6cbb3af953d7ce2"},"suggested_fix":"Give the provider the run's limits (a field set by the driver or from RunPolicy) and the hub's ContentLimits when the daemon wires it (Task 14).","summary":"A browser test's screenshots are scaled to DEFAULT_IMAGE_SIDE (8000), not to the run's RunLimits::image_side, and kept under ContentLimits::default(), not the hub's configured content limits","supersedes":"a395ac41f19b8452ef897ca131981f4f5ed3f97a07e950984faf7bb22be4ed50","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/spend.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T02:55:31.744483Z","id":"b98808c2dc7f38c411fd422c0e84f104d7635678bfa614c7c5da28da339085e2","body":{"detail":"Recorded again where the code now is: it was record a602eba5 on crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs (check 2's refusal), which moved here as spend::disabled for every charged call, web and browser alike. The refusal is the run loop's to journal (Answer::refused(...).uncharged()), made before any entry is, so its call event carries cost_milli: 0 whether or not the row could be written. The attempt is abandoned either way (the claim is lost), no step commits it, and no test reaches it. Keeping the old event would cost a read of the run for each such refusal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":323},"end":{"line":336},"content_hash":"ea3fcc1476218ca1affc0c20fa1d6f1dde7d114d07cdb59516945777a0097a7f"},"summary":"A refusal of step 2 made while the driver no longer holds the run shows a cost of 0 in its event, where the code before the seam showed none","supersedes":"360169087ad793b4a344bec8644d63b6891959c7a7fd85f9ce5a9c9b280e990e","tags":["t5","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/spend.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T02:55:32.073721Z","id":"d6a4c70f957d5094fec65dfb4f0495a1a2829af3d4a63a051df1778ca3f4c984","body":{"detail":"Recorded again where the code now is: it was record 285218bc on crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs; the order is now the Spend sequence's, step 6 (free answers) before step 7 (cap), spec 2026-11-19-claxbot-browser §4.6. A fetch of a URL the run's page store keeps answers from the store even when the fetch cap is reached, because spec 2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools §6.2 says such a fetch does not count against the fetch cap. Checking the cap first would refuse later windows of a page the run already paid for with web_cap. Tests: crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs the_second_window_comes_from_the_store, a_stored_page_is_served_at_the_fetch_cap.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":443},"end":{"line":455},"content_hash":"001d239baca282e2d9741a9a070102b9aa9a9a54922ed0ac028e57cf59a65ba0"},"summary":"The page store is checked before the run's cap, not after it","supersedes":"d4af66f34654b30290184b7ccc1991c404c295916a3bf1227ab20f4e69cfea1b","tags":["t5","revisit:the cap is meant to bound reads of stored pages too","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/web.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T02:55:32.457369Z","id":"0f3fe35b683123d52c15f274de53bbc3e318a2a3ae0255a2c29bb88dcf20c67a","body":{"detail":"It decides whether a search's bot.spend record keeps the provider's response whole or trimmed. It bounds no run and the model reads none of it, so it is not among RunLimits (crates/clax-bot/src/policy.rs); it is a limit of the web surface's own, and moves with the web performer. Re-anchored after the Spend path moved the performer's code (commit 91de6f4a7).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":109},"end":{"line":111},"content_hash":"2bd3a7fd210c42b9e598a581c9f44b2cc45735e7da2b18c33c6e93b9ae941d8f"},"summary":"`AUDIT_RESPONSE_BYTES` (64 KiB) is a size compiled into the web performer","supersedes":"32589555b90c3cd1c487fdf894186ba4dbb25d9673fb7159633336ed8c0c9cff","tags":["for-t5","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:08:08.283596Z","id":"8e4154820752403a67ce5c327387bcff7fedba01c65f5bc4f23a282661630f01","body":{"detail":"Spec §18.4 says neither is charged. price_cap gives time_cap(0) for them and out_of_credits skips closing the session for them (is_cap_call), but no test in crates/clax-bot/tests/browser.rs runs a share with no credits left; if the price step refuses a zero cap when credits are at or below zero, a revoke (which only gives up authority) would be refused credits_exhausted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1048},"end":{"line":1056},"content_hash":"3ae182bc2ee67498e3ae5f4b14139e5271bd299d09835dbae711ec98f04f9b91"},"summary":"A share or revoke still passes Spend's price step with a zero-second browser.time cap: untested whether a person whose credits are exhausted can share or revoke","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:52:29.553432Z","id":"620589900acbe449c3fe244c8c18c6e2946e3ff025c55c405a0310209dd007cd","body":{"detail":"SessionOp::perform calls leave_policy for every goto (clax/browser.rs:1086-1101), and leave_policy checks scope.allowed(url) only when BrowserSessions::leaves answers true (clax/browser.rs:1381-1400). leaves answers false for any session with no synthetic origin, so for every URL session (live.rs:531-551, `None => false`). Nothing else checks the goto: SessionOp::admit (clax/browser.rs:1011-1045) checks only the capability and runTests, and the only other caller of BrowseScope::allowed is the open (clax/browser.rs:608-610). The goto is then held only by BrowsePolicy's per-request check (browse.rs BrowseScope::refusal), which checks scheme, private or local hosts, own hosts and admits_host. It does not check: the URL itself under `sender` (any path and query on a host of the sender's URLs passes, where §4.5 admits only URLs the sender wrote), the source under `allowlist`, admit's looks_credentialed refusal (web/access.rs:380), and PublicUrl's credentials and 2,000-character limits. browse.rs:8-17 says BrowseScope::allowed governs 'The start URL and each goto'; spec §8.5 says a goto elsewhere 'from a session of any kind' must pass the rule. The page can already reach the same hosts through evaluate or a click (browse.rs:36-40 makes host-level bounding the egress guarantee), so the practical effect is that the URL-level rule and the credential check stop at the open. That is a contract the docs state and the code does not keep.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1374},"end":{"line":1401},"content_hash":"d701af3d81f30979680867f2c9d6777032727ed1bfa719dc52a5215674485878"},"suggested_fix":"Either check every goto of a URL session against the session's BrowseScope (keep the scope on the session, or rebuild it as leave_policy does) and refuse with the rule's code, adding a test that a goto under `sender` to an unwritten URL on a sender host is url_not_in_prior_context; or, if host-level is the intended contract, change browse.rs's module docs and spec §8.5 to say a URL session's goto is held to the hosts alone, and keep the credentialed-URL check for gotos.","summary":"A page.goto in a URL session is never checked against browser.open.url's URL rule, only against the page-request host filter, though browse.rs's module docs and spec §8.5 say each goto passes the rule","tags":["review","review:browser-unify","security","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:54:51.879341Z","id":"785eaa0c0f55f9a3e624ac3dfae27ce4dd9e7ce30bfd3187597a349930e04e33","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:1086-1101 calls leave_policy for each goto; leave_policy (1379-1401) returns Ok(None) before scope.allowed when BrowserSessions::leaves is false, and crates/clax-bot/src/browser/live.rs:540-541 answers false for any session with synthetic None (every URL session). In the task, live.rs:979-1001 checks goto only when synthetic is Some. The only non-test callers of BrowseScope::allowed are clax/browser.rs:610 (the open) and 1400 (leave_policy). BrowsePolicy::decide (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs:266-281) calls BrowseScope::refusal (184-211), which checks scheme, local hosts, own hosts and admits_host only, so no path/query match under sender, no source under allowlist, no Refused::Credentialed and no PublicUrl length or credential check. browse.rs:7-18 says BrowseScope::allowed governs 'The start URL and each goto', and spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md:1222-1223 says a goto elsewhere 'from a session of any kind' must pass the rule. The egress bound is still host-level (browse.rs:36-40), so concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"620589900acbe449c3fe244c8c18c6e2946e3ff025c55c405a0310209dd007cd","summary":"confirmed: a goto in a URL session is never run through BrowseScope::allowed, only through BrowsePolicy's host-level per-request check","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/spend.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:55:40.561020Z","id":"899aef6cc2ce06191908566c1501d79e794e10bab24153470a579cc6ba90e88a","body":{"detail":"Step 2 checks the binding has the operation, but the three browser.open kinds share browser.open and the session operations (crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs Bindings::clax, CLAX_GRANTED). Step 3 (spend.rs:413-421) reads Capabilities::now for the person and never intersects it with bot_runs.caps. So a run made with browser.open.artifact alone, after the admin grants browser.open.url, opens clax.browser.open({url}); and leave_policy (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:1378-1400) converts an artifact session to a URL session on the live grant the same way. Spec section 4.3 defines caps(run) over declared(run) and section 4.4 says 'A capability granted mid-run is not added'. The two halves then disagree: crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs reevaluate_browser filters CapSet::parse(&run.caps), so the next grant or revoke anywhere on the instance closes that session revoked though nothing it needed was revoked. The test an_open_of_a_kind_the_run_lacks_is_disabled (crates/clax-bot/tests/browser.rs:1679) passes only because its admin offers just the declared kind (run_with_caps, crates/clax-bot/tests/common/mod.rs:720).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":413},"end":{"line":421},"content_hash":"00e4c790411e8887834e9544a57c02f5db6a8a38d25396dd0bc0ae94bf5bb007"},"suggested_fix":"In fresh, refuse <family>_disabled when CapSet::parse(&s.run.caps) lacks c, before the live check; in leave_policy, give no leave policy unless the run declared browser.open.url; add a test that grants browser.open.url mid-run to a run declared with the artifact kind and expects browser_disabled for both an open on a URL and a goto out.","summary":"Step 3 checks a browser capability is live for the person, not that the run declared it: a browser.open kind granted mid-run can be opened","tags":["review","review:browser-unify","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:55:40.561140Z","id":"a31c5dcebae6657f432de6419fe1bd1c3a2dddf076dddba3bbb9679fb781f4a1","body":{"detail":"SessionOp::price_cap is time_cap(call_seconds) (and Open::price_cap at browser.rs:641-643 the same); spend.rs priced compares only that quantity with the week's credits left. Spec section 10.3: 'Before each call: the person can pay for the time not yet charged, the call's time cap, and the idle time (what the session may cost before it is next seen); else credits_exhausted'. The time not yet charged is every millisecond since the session's charged_ms point, the model's turns included (up to browser.session.idle_seconds, default 300 s): a person with credits for 60 s passes the check after a 280 s model turn and the call's segment then charges 280 s or more, past their credits. Likewise an idle end charged by Store::end_bot_browser_session is never preceded by a check that the idle time could be paid. Nothing in clax/browser.rs or clax/spend.rs reads idle_seconds.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1048},"end":{"line":1056},"content_hash":"3ae182bc2ee67498e3ae5f4b14139e5271bd299d09835dbae711ec98f04f9b91"},"suggested_fix":"For a session call, make the price cap's quantity (now_ms - charged_ms) + call_seconds*1000 + idle_seconds*1000, reading charged_ms from the session's row and the session's current point from the registry (BrowserSessions has no per-session 'now' in milliseconds since the open yet: now_ms is Unix time); for an open, call_seconds + idle_seconds. Test a call after a long gap with credits for less than the gap.","summary":"A session call's price check covers only one call's time cap, not the session's uncharged time or its idle time, so a person can be charged past their credits","tags":["review","review:browser-unify","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:55:40.561225Z","id":"58ec6ea93e639ce1b4fbf866171f7d8f966d8932b704b205371728b2cdb7ea5c","body":{"detail":"Priced::usage (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/spend.rs) prices each segment with row_credits_milli, which rounds up once per row (crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs:274-314, div_ceil_checked). At the seeded line (25 micro-USD a second, INFRA_MARGIN_BP 9,000) and the default credit price of 10,000 micro-USD (bot_settings.rs CreditPriceMicroUsd) a browser second costs 4.75 milli-credits, so every segment shorter than about 210 ms is charged 1 milli-credit: a script making 100 locator calls of 30 ms each is charged 100 milli-credits for about 14 milli-credits of time. Spec section 10.3: 'Quantities are milliseconds: nothing is rounded up per call, so many short calls cost what their time costs'. The quantity is kept in milliseconds; the rounding happens in credits.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1117},"end":{"line":1128},"content_hash":"6407b04781847821d6bdf25cc27074685e718980bc86a1fa7e0ae34703689341"},"suggested_fix":"Charge a session's segment as credits(through_ms) - credits(charged_ms), each computed from the session's whole charged time with one ceiling, so the rounding is made once per session rather than per call (the store can compute it in apply_session and end_bot_browser_session, where both points are known); or keep a sub-milli remainder on bot_browser_sessions.","summary":"Each browser segment is its own usage row rounded up to a whole milli-credit, so many short calls cost several times their time","tags":["review","review:browser-unify","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:55:40.561299Z","id":"69059ff9d04e1df872967124142bfe31b4804c21c0918041480659be79bd9846","body":{"detail":"whole_seconds is applied at browser.rs:755 (a failed open, measured from `began`, before source.open, so it also counts the connect time before the WebSocket's upgrade), at 1560 (an abandoned test) and at 1643 (every test). Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md section 10.3 says 'Quantities are milliseconds: nothing is rounded up per call' and 'browser.test is one call: its segment is its whole session'; section 10.3 also starts an open's segment at the WebSocket's upgrade. The module docs (browser.rs:48-49, 'rounded up to the second') state the first version's rule. Each test is overcharged up to 999 ms; the test time_is_charged_by_the_whole_second holds the old rule.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":113},"end":{"line":117},"content_hash":"481b331a1c2902b4ca38c1ccca0d01e20861c8c80ebbc5dc07bec92565bbc979"},"suggested_fix":"Charge the measured milliseconds (capped by the call's time cap) in all three places, measure a failed open from the transport's return (when the browser opened) rather than from before source.open, drop whole_seconds and its test, and update the module docs.","summary":"A test, an open that failed after its browser opened, and an abandoned test are charged their time rounded up to the whole second, which spec section 10.3 rules out","tags":["review","review:browser-unify","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:55:40.561367Z","id":"47a5f86ed72f97d82070ac91a186b65fe10f408403a70eec7a11483a79daf042","body":{"detail":"BrowserSessions::open puts the session in the registry and the browser is running before the Open performer writes SessionSpend::Open. Two paths leave it unrecorded: (1) priced.usage fails (browser.rs:713-715, Finish::refused with no session), or spend::write's Store::spend_journaled fails (run_not_claimed, step_mismatch, a store error; spend.rs write answers Answer::unwritten) - nothing closes the session and the script never receives its handle; (2) the host ends it between the open's answer and its write (a revoke's reevaluate_browser, a lost page): the task's mark hands the end to the charger at once (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/live.rs:853-873), Store::end_bot_browser_session finds no row and charges nothing (crates/clax-store/src/bot_web.rs:691-693), then the open's write inserts an open row that nothing ever closes (end_run and close_unheld skip a session the registry has ended) until the next daemon start marks it lost. In (1) the browser runs uncharged until the step commits and close_unheld drops it, and meanwhile open_sessions counts it against browser.max_open_per_run (default 1), so a step that retries its open answers browser_cap and has no handle to close. Spec section 10.3 charges each millisecond once.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":700},"end":{"line":745},"content_hash":"9cfdf4bb013e4b46133e66ed9b9a5dcda49b4c73747df748b7f429f631eeb4d2"},"suggested_fix":"When an Open's Finish carries no SessionSpend, or its write fails, close the session with the host's end (a reason such as `lost` or a new `unwritten`) and charge it through an end that inserts the row when none exists (end_bot_browser_session given the kind and opened_at from Ended); or have the registry hold an end made before the open is acknowledged as written and charge it after.","summary":"An open whose Spend is not written leaves its session open with no row: its time is never charged and it holds the run's open slot","tags":["review","review:browser-unify","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:55:40.561441Z","id":"2d9eaf18d8471017626c2e796d410bdde5b8a3c1f707f723e2b4b47d52b7b18f","body":{"detail":"browser.close sends Msg::Close(Closed); the task's mark (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/live.rs:853-873) queues no Ended for SessionEnd::Closed, since the close's own Spend (SessionSpend::Close) is to charge it. If Store::spend_journaled then refuses (run_not_claimed after a lost lease, step_mismatch, a store error), spend::write answers Answer::unwritten and nothing is written: the session's row stays open with its old charged_ms, the step run again answers browser_session_closed (the registry's reason) uncharged, BrowserSessions::end_run and close_unheld skip it because e.ended is set, and only the next daemon start closes the row, as lost, charging nothing. The segment from the last charged point to the close is never charged, against spec section 10.3 ('close charges it in its own Spend transaction'; each millisecond once).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1076},"end":{"line":1080},"content_hash":"1955cf4d88f045f03d3ce365ce87d54a6d728ad6a4f0af048c7346ba2999e356"},"suggested_fix":"On a close's failed write, charge the tail with Store::end_bot_browser_session(run, session, at_ms, Closed), which charges only while the row is open; or have end_run also end, through end_bot_browser_session, every row of the run the store still holds open at the point the registry closed it.","summary":"A browser.close whose Spend fails is never charged: the registry has ended the session and nothing charges its last segment","tags":["review","review:browser-unify","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:55:40.561508Z","id":"02828e65bd288f2b745956ebde66f700a5afae8e861a2189a17173b23eb38472","body":{"detail":"Spec section 11.1 gives browser.open.url.max_per_run as 'sessions on a URL, gotos out included' (and section 4.2's cap for browser.open.url, 'sessions on a URL'). leave_policy checks the URL rule and nothing else, and SessionOp's count_key is ('browser.session.call', u32::MAX); the converting call's entry has no counted or count_as (browser.rs:1186-1201). So a run under max_per_run 5 for URLs and 10 for the clax opens 10 artifact sessions and converts each with page.goto, holding 15 sessions on the web. The module docs (browser.rs:26-28) say calls on a session are not counted, without the exception.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1378},"end":{"line":1400},"content_hash":"36932d00d797a7e98fe13caec85e720ab321d66ff46d26316c0f84e2858cb0de"},"suggested_fix":"In leave_policy, refuse browser_cap when seen.count(\"browser.open.url\") has reached the URL capability's max_per_run, and mark the converting call's entry counted with count_as browser.open.url; add a test converting past the cap.","summary":"A goto out of an artifact or content session is not counted against browser.open.url.max_per_run","tags":["review","review:browser-unify","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/spend.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T06:00:15.653664Z","id":"55d5f03d4f78e2184c7b9c8ef4fb00911955d6adcf012bfd01437c0bd3c2703a","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/spend.rs:385 (step 2) checks s.cx.binding.has(call.op), and crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs:270-279 CLAX_GRANTED grants browser.open and the session operations for any of OPEN_CAPS, so an artifact-only run's binding has browser.open. spend.rs:413-421 (step 3) takes Capabilities::now(store, &run.person, ..) and caps.get(c) with c = cap_of(kind_of_source(args)) (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:522-524); crates/clax-bot/src/capability.rs:367-403 reads only grants and switches, never the run. The only read of s.run.caps in clax/ is browser.rs:791, which picks the capability named in a refusal for an unknown session. leave_policy (browser.rs:1378-1400) gives a URL policy whenever seen.caps.get(Capability::OpenUrl) is Ok. crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs:1349-1368 reevaluate_browser does filter CapSet::parse(&run.caps), so the two disagree as described. Spec section 4.4 (lines 296-301): 'A capability granted mid-run is not added'.","kind":"comment","references":"899aef6cc2ce06191908566c1501d79e794e10bab24153470a579cc6ba90e88a","summary":"confirmed: step 3 reads only the person's live capabilities; nothing on the call path intersects them with bot_runs.caps","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T06:00:15.655059Z","id":"1fac37d781fdcde133f87c10254feb4f45e4d324985d32e2112da2f400670070","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:1048-1056 SessionOp::price_cap is time_cap(call_seconds) (0 for a share or revoke), browser.rs:640-642 Open::price_cap is time_cap(call_seconds); crates/clax-bot/src/clax/spend.rs:470-512 priced compares priced.usage(cap.qty) alone with s.week_left(). The segment actually charged is through - charged_ms (browser.rs:1114-1121), which includes the time since the last call. `grep -n idle_seconds crates/clax-bot/src/clax/*.rs` prints nothing. Spec section 10.3 (line 1317): 'Before each call: the person can pay for the time not yet charged, the call's time cap, and the idle time'.","kind":"comment","references":"a31c5dcebae6657f432de6419fe1bd1c3a2dddf076dddba3bbb9679fb781f4a1","summary":"confirmed: the step 8 check prices only one call's time cap; the uncharged gap and the idle time are not in it","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T06:00:15.656247Z","id":"3e9c11d971b7f9307665a9fbad3e704ed824bff48152d8018c088eb02537ebd6","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/spend.rs:174-192 Priced::usage calls row_credits_milli for each segment; crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs:286-313 rounds up once per call (div_ceil_checked). Seeded line: BROWSER_SECOND_COST_MICRO_USD 25 at INFRA_MARGIN_BP 9,000 (credits.rs:561, 1017-1033), Unit::BrowserSecond base 1,000 (credits.rs:137), CreditPriceMicroUsd default 10,000 (crates/clax-store/src/bot_settings.rs:81): 25 x 19,000 x 1,000 / (10,000 x 10,000 x 1,000) = 4.75 milli-credits a second, so a 30 ms segment (0.1425) is charged 1 milli-credit and any segment under about 210 ms is charged at least 1. Spec section 10.3 (line 1315): 'nothing is rounded up per call, so many short calls cost what their time costs'.","kind":"comment","references":"58ec6ea93e639ce1b4fbf866171f7d8f966d8932b704b205371728b2cdb7ea5c","summary":"confirmed: each segment is priced through row_credits_milli, which takes one ceiling per row","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T06:00:15.657415Z","id":"4f5399e003bc9a85da603efa9a48d3068e5666824506309572cf730c38c5c2d6","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:113-116 whole_seconds is (ms + 999) / 1000 * 1000, applied at browser.rs:755 (failed open, ms from `began`, taken at 693 before sessions.open), 1560 (abandoned test) and 1643 (test). Module docs browser.rs:48-49: 'A test is charged its measured time, rounded up to the second'. Test browser.rs:1732 time_is_charged_by_the_whole_second asserts whole_seconds(4_200) == 5_000. Spec section 10.3 lines 1300, 1315 and 1322.","kind":"comment","references":"69059ff9d04e1df872967124142bfe31b4804c21c0918041480659be79bd9846","summary":"confirmed: whole_seconds rounds a failed open, an abandoned test and every test up to the second","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T06:00:43.757712Z","id":"b0ced927aaafa0b513d06b88a9f6f234098995122bfc645099d88e923c1f993d","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:694-715: sessions.open has started the browser and registered the session before priced.usage, whose failure returns Finish::refused with no session. A failed Store::spend_journaled leaves the call unwritten (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/spend.rs write). Either way the registry entry stays with ended None, counted by open_sessions (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/live.rs:676-683) in Open::admit's max_open_per_run check (browser.rs:590-603). Its later end goes through Task::mark (live.rs:853-873) to the charger, and Store::end_bot_browser_session (crates/clax-store/src/bot_web.rs:681-693) returns 0 when session_in finds no row. In the race of path (2), apply_session's Open arm (bot_web.rs:307, 336-349) inserts a row after that end; end_run and close_unheld (live.rs:469-505) select only e.ended.is_none(), so the row stays open until the start-time lost sweep (bot_web.rs:740-754), which charges nothing (test at bot_web.rs:1769, 'a lost session charges nothing').","kind":"comment","references":"47a5f86ed72f97d82070ac91a186b65fe10f408403a70eec7a11483a79daf042","summary":"confirmed: an open left unwritten keeps a registry session with no store row, and its end charges nothing","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T06:00:43.759102Z","id":"1dd47111bed95523fb5c9e4c750d15bf461c327088b9c201a3746b75f8b09a6f","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:1076-1080 closes with SessionEnd::Closed before the Spend write; crates/clax-bot/src/browser/live.rs:853-859 Task::mark sets e.ended and queues no Ended when reason == SessionEnd::Closed. If the write then fails, the row keeps its old charged_ms. The step run again gets ended_error from sender (live.rs:734-740); end_run and close_unheld (live.rs:469-505) select only sessions with ended None; end_run's retain (live.rs:473) then drops it. The row stays open until the start sweep marks it lost (crates/clax-store/src/bot_web.rs:740-754), and a lost session charges nothing (bot_web.rs:1769). Spec section 10.3 line 1309: 'close charges it in its own Spend transaction'.","kind":"comment","references":"2d9eaf18d8471017626c2e796d410bdde5b8a3c1f707f723e2b4b47d52b7b18f","summary":"confirmed: a close whose Spend fails ends the session in the registry and nothing charges its tail","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T06:00:43.760464Z","id":"396207a10a2630f301eda4decf615effd8892d4c91052fe246e39a7661074a4f","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:1378-1400 leave_policy checks the URL rule only; SessionOp::count_key (browser.rs:1044-1046) is ('browser.session.call', u32::MAX); the call's Finish (browser.rs:1192-1201) sets no counted, so counted_as adds no count_as and crates/clax-store/src/bot_web.rs:816-832 bot_spend_counts never counts it under browser.open.url. Spec section 11.1 table: browser.open.url.max_per_run 'sessions on a URL, gotos out included'. Module docs browser.rs:26-28 say calls on a session are not counted.","kind":"comment","references":"02828e65bd288f2b745956ebde66f700a5afae8e861a2189a17173b23eb38472","summary":"confirmed: a goto out is never counted against browser.open.url.max_per_run","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:06:46.172268Z","id":"ed06576a8ce7d20b9cb251338349756538e8f3f7e767b57e49be0b9d2ce0b152","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"47a5f86ed72f97d82070ac91a186b65fe10f408403a70eec7a11483a79daf042","summary":"Partly fixed in 94f51d4c2: an open whose usage cannot be priced or whose Spend is not written is closed dropped and charged through Store::end_unwritten_bot_browser_session (test browser::an_open_whose_spend_fails_closes_and_charges_its_session, //crates/clax-bot:integration). Still open: a host end between the open's answer and its write leaves no end time in the registry to charge at","tags":["review:browser-unify","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:06:46.175863Z","id":"03d472536e748122f512aa7837769c825bc9fa2c87703dc5d29e2bc7d33d2785","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a31c5dcebae6657f432de6419fe1bd1c3a2dddf076dddba3bbb9679fb781f4a1","summary":"Not fixed: the check spec §10.3 describes needs the registry to know each session's uncharged time at the call (BrowserSessions keeps no per-session clock point for it) and raises every credit threshold a session call meets by idle_seconds' worth (300 s by default). Which bound to apply before a call (the call's cap alone, plus the uncharged time, plus the idle time) is a pricing choice for the owner","tags":["review:browser-unify","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:06:46.176855Z","id":"45761f4f5e9116ea745da03777b056b035a46513868de43327f384ea39c53288","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"58ec6ea93e639ce1b4fbf866171f7d8f966d8932b704b205371728b2cdb7ea5c","summary":"Not fixed: rounding once per session means charging each segment as credits(through) minus credits(charged) over the session's whole time (or keeping a sub-milli-credit remainder on bot_browser_sessions), which changes what a call's answer reports as its cost. Which of the two, and what a call's cost then says, is a pricing choice for the owner","tags":["review:browser-unify","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:35:26.778475Z","id":"a8c7f63848f137cc1491c1f2d16c8031cd338a7ea6ef186c0442f8d45c072ca2","body":{"detail":"`policy` reads `self.tick.clax.created` (217) and `Tick::script` reads `self.clax.base` (554). Both are `clax::Tally` fields (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/tally.rs 21-37), folded by the tick (run.rs 1052). A `clax` session opened by `SurfaceProvider::begin` should fold them itself from `StepCx::history`, as the proof's adapter now does with the same function (crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs 159), and the tick's copy then has no reader in this file. `Tally::of` reads only steps whose `committed_at` is set; `StepCx::history` is documented as the committed steps (surface.rs 606-610), and the tick's `steps` may hold a second uncommitted step if a run ever had two (only the first is taken out as `open`, run.rs 1041-1044), so pass the slice as it is and let the fold filter. Mutations that show both reads are held: 554 as `self.run.base_version` fails `golden::resumed::a_script_after_a_publish_is_resumed_from_the_published_version` and `seam::a_script_after_a_rebase_starts_from_the_version_rebased_onto`; 217 without the tally's `created` fails `rules::a_brief_run_creates_one_artifact` and `golden::scripts::a_second_artifact_is_refused`.\n\nRe-recorded unchanged from record 7564590a on crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs, whose subject moved here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":241},"end":{"line":244},"content_hash":"6b3ae9ea2f79eb1ad2baa17775c07b4ff2f4187e34a0a23f16d8632096698d61"},"summary":"For the change that moves script.rs behind the seam: the two reads of `Tick::clax` here (217, 554) become the clax session's own `Tally::of(cx.history)`","supersedes":"e44906117bbe90a86bb17433bc01292276a818fb96139ae002e39205a37647e2","tags":["t3","for-t5","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:35:27.000717Z","id":"cfe851a7bb3b8766a040a3c60ad85894bcfb467a903968a3fa81d4760eb708d4","body":{"detail":"Every script the proof runs is step 2 of its run, after one turn: `tally` (seam.rs 102-111) always answers `(None, false)` and `begin` (145-163) always loads the draft at the run's own base. Changes made one at a time and run with `bazel test //crates/clax-bot:integration --test_arg=seam::` (7 tests): (1) seam.rs 148 loads the draft at `run.base_version` whatever `tally` answers: all 7 pass. (2) seam.rs 238 drops `self.created_before`: all 7 pass. (3) seam.rs 320 never refuses a second publish in one script: all 7 pass. (4) seam.rs 215 hands `OpCtx::new` another attempt: all 7 pass (the fake host does not read it; crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs 633 does). The same changes made to today's code and run against the whole of `//crates/clax-bot:integration` (175 tests): script.rs 217 without `self.tick.hist.created` fails `golden::scripts::a_second_artifact_is_refused` and `rules::a_brief_run_creates_one_artifact`; script.rs 301 fails `golden::scripts::the_draft_operations_answers_are_pinned`; but script.rs 554 as `let base = self.run.base_version;` passes all 175, the seam's 7 among them, and passes `//crates/clax-bot:all`, `//crates/clax-server:all` and `//crates/clax-worker:bot_test` too. No test runs a script after a step that published or rebased: crates/clax-bot/tests/rules.rs 143-197 rebases and publishes in the run's last script. So the change that moves script.rs 554-555 into a provider's `begin` can load every later script's draft at the run's first base (a second publish then conflicts, and a script after a rebase reads the old files) and pass the proof and every fixture under crates/clax-bot/tests/golden/.\n\nRe-recorded unchanged from record 487f98c0 on crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs, whose subject moved here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":241},"end":{"line":260},"content_hash":"03343b8f0b9d8e81911ac21e78ea1ca8865b8cad479155c5bf23d81e2e7dd508"},"suggested_fix":"A proof case, and a fixture for today's path, in which a first script publishes (and another in which it rebases) and a second script reads a file, writes and publishes: the second step's draft, its `if_version` and its `payload.base` compared on both paths. For a brief's run, a second script that calls `artifacts.create` after a first that created one.","summary":"No proof case opens a session over a history that moved the draft's base or created an artifact, so what `begin` folds from the committed steps is unproved, and for the base no other test of clax-bot holds it either","supersedes":"b8e71a2cec89ce672794e3030882a91f62d4301879f4eaf4b67834ba96d79318","tags":["review","seam","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:35:27.225898Z","id":"a3f97a13d6d123931cda486692c46a5e2188cf1b702edd78dfc06a7d5ddd0ea7","body":{"detail":"`policy` reads `self.tick.clax.created` (217) and `Tick::script` reads `self.clax.base` (554). Both are `clax::Tally` fields (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/tally.rs 21-37), folded by the tick (run.rs 1052). A `clax` session opened by `SurfaceProvider::begin` should fold them itself from `StepCx::history`, as the proof's adapter now does with the same function (crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs 159), and the tick's copy then has no reader in this file. `Tally::of` reads only steps whose `committed_at` is set; `StepCx::history` is documented as the committed steps (surface.rs 606-610), and the tick's `steps` may hold a second uncommitted step if a run ever had two (only the first is taken out as `open`, run.rs 1041-1044), so pass the slice as it is and let the fold filter. Mutations that show both reads are held: 554 as `self.run.base_version` fails `golden::resumed::a_script_after_a_publish_is_resumed_from_the_published_version` and `seam::a_script_after_a_rebase_starts_from_the_version_rebased_onto`; 217 without the tally's `created` fails `rules::a_brief_run_creates_one_artifact` and `golden::scripts::a_second_artifact_is_refused`.\n\nRecorded again where the code now is: it was record 7564590a4493710cb151474667f770e3c09df7943ba45796371ac003bf16eaed on crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs, whose lines moved to this file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":243},"end":{"line":244},"content_hash":"6d8ae587df767f4b4d0cb20618cf56c2ea4b0ef14a847a74dc2598a4cbb0cef3"},"summary":"For the change that moves script.rs behind the seam: the two reads of `Tick::clax` here (217, 554) become the clax session's own `Tally::of(cx.history)`","supersedes":"f6bc4e8fec82aa61650c6347e56085d7883e14c313a264c3dbd60876e980a10c","tags":["t3","for-t5","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:35:27.451325Z","id":"a0e9bed96bb5b7566d333997c4d3c3393e429441aabf55dcebdb7924fdbeab06","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs still calls `BotHost::working` (before a turn or a script, and after each terminal commit) and posts every notice itself (`notify_at`). crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs calls no provider's `working`: row 1 of the step table in surface.rs says so. For the change that moves the endings: the run loop calls `working`, `ending` and `ended` for every binding; the conformance fixture of this provider (crates/clax-bot/tests/providers.rs) then has an `ending` that can fail and notices to read, and the two cases it names as not applicable are played; and a run whose scripts reach another surface (crates/clax-bot/tests/generic.rs) still ends with Clax's notices on Clax's threads, because only its script step is generic.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":262},"end":{"line":298},"content_hash":"161f4416ff22cdfa8c84cf4e902f4229d134a799a0ae90e8e0c2331efe335086"},"summary":"Clax's provider does nothing in `working`, `ending` and `ended`: the roster and the notices are still the run loop's","supersedes":"605dcd1c00f980ef5797e5a87538ef7afa971998e2db061f0dacd722b67c93f0","tags":["t5","for-t7","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:35:27.676271Z","id":"a8cab792828da16d3e79f52d8001955cb2eb7db31021f34c67c7a4fd859119f5","body":{"detail":"Commits ac72d8527 and 359f0c1f4; see the reply on record d311ae86 (crates/clax-bot/src/registry.rs). `host::host_op` (crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs) checks that the operation is one of src/clax.d.ts with the access asked. Left open for the owner to close.","kind":"comment","references":"8320f2cf8d7130eda31cd5a453323a0ae3f6a7b060213b2cdbc71aab3002f540","span":{"start":{"line":93},"end":{"line":97},"content_hash":"7c64c4ec37072d9b071617065da0502686ca4854cd798312e8cffe6eb54bbaa4"},"summary":"Done: the session names its own operations (`PARTS`, `Part`), and `api::Performer`, `Deps.host` and `Deps.web` are gone","supersedes":"5c41a158fbcbf6646a6b618b93366aacf7c753057742999ad3523fa3f9feeb23","tags":["t10","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/clax/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:35:27.905225Z","id":"05f9704bad7387a30c1d500f2dfb65a31118eac580720d80cab377a7e49c8291","body":{"detail":"`api::Performer`: this match, by which a session finds the part that performs an operation; `host::check_op` (crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs), for a `BotHost`'s own check; the table and its tests in api.rs; and the reference. `Deps::host`: run.rs (the roster's `working`, the notices' `plan_reply`, the request's `context`), driver.rs (`start_waiting`) and `ClaxProvider::of`. `Deps::web`: `ClaxProvider::of` alone. A provider that names its own operations (a match on the operation's name here) frees `Performer`; `Deps::host` and `Deps::web` go when the tick is given its providers and the roster and notices are theirs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":154},"content_hash":"246a016da1e82e056a9a4bc78190c89922d142312dda87775aea74aee6086e31"},"summary":"What still reads `api::Performer`, `Deps::host` and `Deps::web`","supersedes":"8320f2cf8d7130eda31cd5a453323a0ae3f6a7b060213b2cdbc71aab3002f540","tags":["t5","for-t10","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
